From: bvchess <53128914+bvchess@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:32:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] The example restricted gains the subcommands
 fix-smooth, smooth-tree and census for the study of the smooth part of a
 proof (lab/work/core5060), and every search a score to beat: with --above S a
 search starts from an incumbent worth S that holds no set, run by the engine
 as search::search runs it, so that it proves no game of the restriction
 scores more or finds the best one that does, and the lines give the GF(2)
 bound of the root and of the restricted root.  fix-smooth fixes or bars the
 B-smooth candidates (the smooth part) as the committed set of a game has
 them, with flips, and searches the rest; smooth-tree decides the smooth part
 member by member under the GF(2) bound, by Knuth's estimator with the leaves
 searched, or walked whole with the search's incremental bound (checked
 against the bound from the root every thousandth node) and every leaf
 searched, a proof when every leaf's search finishes, or estimated from a
 random sample of its frontier with a time limit; census counts, through the
 search's trace, the conflicts a search branches on by depth and by largest
 prime.  window shares its split of the candidates with fix-smooth, and
 run_all returns any result on threads with room for the walk

